WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.445 --> 00:00:07.966
Hello, everyone!

2
00:00:08.026 --> 00:00:22.275
Faye Moss here with another episode of Superstars in History, where I interview the legends of the past.

3
00:00:23.135 --> 00:00:30.660
In the 1980s and 1990s, today's guest was the most photographed, most famous woman in the world!

4
00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:38.817
She modernized the British royal family with her sense of style, concern for everyone, and efforts to introduce

5
00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:40.739
her children to the real world.

6
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.985
Please give a warm welcome to Diana, Princess of Wales!

7
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.401
Hello, Faye!

8
00:01:05.001 --> 00:01:06.722
I understand your grandmother is sick.

9
00:01:07.162 --> 00:01:09.264
How's she doing, and how are you?

10
00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:11.926
She's getting better, thanks.

11
00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:14.307
That's so kind of you to ask.

12
00:01:14.928 --> 00:01:18.530
Then again you were known for your kindness, even as a child.

13
00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:24.854
You were born in 1961 and came to public attention later as Lady Diana Spencer.

14
00:01:25.455 --> 00:01:26.755
Tell us about your family.

15
00:01:29.157 --> 00:01:33.440
The Spencers are one of the oldest, most distinguished families in Great Britain.

16
00:01:34.092 --> 00:01:37.433
The family has been friends with the royal family for generations.

17
00:01:37.953 --> 00:01:42.174
In fact, I grew up on one of the royal family's properties in the countryside.

18
00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:46.475
That must have been a beautiful place to live!

19
00:01:47.616 --> 00:01:51.497
It was, but unfortunately my parents' marriage was troubled.

20
00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:55.878
They divorced when I was seven, and that trauma shaped my whole life.

21
00:01:56.598 --> 00:02:02.600
After a bitter legal battle, my father was granted custody of my two older sisters, my younger brother,

22
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:03.200
and me.

23
00:02:04.716 --> 00:02:08.339
Did you feel different from your friends because your parents were divorced?

24
00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:09.860
Oh, yes!

25
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.302
Hardly anyone got divorced back then.

26
00:02:13.142 --> 00:02:18.867
But there was one positive result: I could always sympathize with people who had family problems.

27
00:02:19.807 --> 00:02:26.392
When I was 13, there was more upheaval because my grandfather died, and my father became Earl Spencer.

28
00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:31.436
We moved two hours away from my friends to live at our family's ancestral home.

29
00:02:32.588 --> 00:02:35.910
Things got worse when my father married someone we all hated!

30
00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:38.752
That's a lot to deal with!

31
00:02:39.452 --> 00:02:41.833
Can you tell us some of your happier memories?

32
00:02:43.134 --> 00:02:44.695
Loved to swim and dive.

33
00:02:45.195 --> 00:02:47.116
Loved tap dancing and ballet.

34
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:51.639
My dream was to become a ballerina, but I grew too tall.

35
00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.681
What did you do after leaving school?

36
00:02:55.681 --> 00:03:00.264
I moved to London and worked as an assistant teacher at a nursery school and a babysitter.

37
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.702
I also cleaned house for my oldest sister, Sarah, and her friends.

38
00:03:05.542 --> 00:03:08.303
You were a cleaner before you married a prince?

39
00:03:08.943 --> 00:03:11.844
That sounds like something from a fairy tale!

40
00:03:12.385 --> 00:03:18.047
And the Prince of Wales is heir to the British throne, so you'd eventually be queen!

41
00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:21.088
What was it like to date Prince Charles?

42
00:03:22.049 --> 00:03:28.571
The British press was always interested in Charles' girlfriends, especially since he was 32, and everyone thought it

43
00:03:28.611 --> 00:03:29.992
was time for him to marry.

44
00:03:30.952 --> 00:03:33.414
They went into a frenzy when we started dating.

45
00:03:34.415 --> 00:03:40.320
Every day dozens of reporters and photographers waited outside my flat and chased my car.

46
00:03:41.341 --> 00:03:47.907
The tabloids called you "Shy Di" because you ducked your head whenever they tried to photograph you.

47
00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:52.671
You were so young and pretty, and everyone loved that you were shy!

48
00:03:52.691 --> 00:03:56.374
I wasn't shy—I was terrified!

49
00:03:56.995 --> 00:04:00.749
I was only 19, but the paparazzi wouldn't leave me alone.

50
00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:06.010
I had no choice but to cope if I wanted the prince to marry me—and I wanted that

51
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:06.810
very much.

52
00:04:07.431 --> 00:04:10.751
As king, Charles would be the head of the Church of England.

53
00:04:11.492 --> 00:04:16.833
I naively thought this meant he couldn't get divorced, so my children would never suffer as I had.

54
00:04:17.313 --> 00:04:19.274
We'd live happily ever after.

55
00:04:20.094 --> 00:04:26.216
More than 750 million people around the world watched your fairy-tale wedding on TV in 1981.

56
00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.861
Did you hope the press would stop hounding you after that?

57
00:04:31.642 --> 00:04:32.302
Of course!

58
00:04:32.742 --> 00:04:35.943
But the wedding only increased interest in everything about me.

59
00:04:37.024 --> 00:04:39.125
Well, you were very stylish.

60
00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:47.908
The rest of the royal family looked rather um old-fashioned, but you were a British fashion icon.

61
00:04:48.969 --> 00:04:52.150
Yes, but I wanted to be known for more than my clothes.

62
00:04:53.011 --> 00:04:57.913
Charles, as heir, had a clearly defined role, but there wasn't one for me.

63
00:04:58.594 --> 00:05:06.521
On our official visits, I gradually realized that I could help people—the sick, the dying, the abused—just by

64
00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:07.201
being there.

65
00:05:07.902 --> 00:05:11.665
People were starving for love, and that was something I could give.

66
00:05:12.886 --> 00:05:18.671
Right. Before you, the royal family was a lot more distant from people, and many people credit you

67
00:05:18.731 --> 00:05:19.992
for updating its image.

68
00:05:20.973 --> 00:05:26.677
I believed the monarchy needed to be relevant to modern people's lives, so I became involved in causes

69
00:05:26.757 --> 00:05:29.018
that the royal family had mostly avoided.

70
00:05:29.679 --> 00:05:34.842
I was honored to be asked to open the first British hospital ward for HIV/AIDS patients.

71
00:05:35.362 --> 00:05:41.305
There was such a huge stigma attached to the disease then that I made international headlines just by

72
00:05:41.405 --> 00:05:42.866
shaking hands with a patient.

73
00:05:43.526 --> 00:05:47.268
You made a big impact, and your fame helped you do it.

74
00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:50.470
But being in the spotlight wasn't easy for you.

75
00:05:51.491 --> 00:05:56.465
Sadly my marriage wasn't very happy since my husband was in love with someone else.

76
00:05:56.985 --> 00:06:03.206
I grew depressed and struggled with an eating disorder, which went on for years until a friend persuaded

77
00:06:03.246 --> 00:06:04.127
me to seek help.

78
00:06:05.007 --> 00:06:09.148
My own experiences gave me great compassion for those with mental illness.

79
00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:15.370
I can't believe we haven't talked about your children yet!

80
00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.730
They were so important to you.

81
00:06:18.491 --> 00:06:19.311
My boys!

82
00:06:19.811 --> 00:06:22.552
William was born in 1982 and Harry, two years later.

83
00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.702
I wanted them to lead normal lives, if possible.

84
00:06:27.303 --> 00:06:33.128
Unlike my husband, they attended school with other children right from the start, and we went to movies

85
00:06:33.288 --> 00:06:34.329
and amusement parks.

86
00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:39.513
You took them to hospitals, hospices, and homeless shelters.

87
00:06:39.974 --> 00:06:42.536
Was that decision influenced by your own work?

88
00:06:43.357 --> 00:06:48.942
Yes, it was especially important for William to see how real people live since he was in the

89
00:06:48.982 --> 00:06:49.942
line of succession.

90
00:06:50.823 --> 00:06:56.765
As for me, I eventually grew tired of the glamorous parts of being Princess of Wales and focused

91
00:06:56.825 --> 00:06:58.066
on my charitable work.

92
00:06:59.006 --> 00:07:00.806
I had no desire to be queen.

93
00:07:02.547 --> 00:07:05.948
Thank you for this refreshingly candid interview.

94
00:07:06.828 --> 00:07:09.129
We'll let you get back to history now.

95
00:07:09.889 --> 00:07:10.749
Thank you, Faye!

96
00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:23.249
Princess Diana's marriage ended in divorce in 1996, but she stayed in the public eye, raising awareness of

97
00:07:23.289 --> 00:07:25.010
the problem of land mines.

98
00:07:26.431 --> 00:07:32.274
The next year she died in a car accident that occurred while her driver was trying to elude

99
00:07:32.314 --> 00:07:33.275
the paparazzi.

100
00:07:33.855 --> 00:07:40.979
The world went into mourning, and huge crowds lined London's streets for her funeral while millions watched on

101
00:07:41.019 --> 00:07:48.743
TV. Now adults with families of their own, Diana's sons continue her legacy of caring and concern for

102
00:07:48.964 --> 00:07:53.274
others. That's all for now on Superstars in History.

103
00:07:53.994 --> 00:07:54.114
I'm
